---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PropsTable from "../../../components/PropsTable.astro";
import Code from "../../../components/Code.astro";

const triggerProps = [
	{ name: "groups", type: "MentionGroup[]", description: "Group order and labels; unlisted groups follow in first-seen order" },
	{ name: "char", type: "string", description: "Trigger character — @, #, /, or any string", required: true },
	{ name: "data", type: "MentionItem[] | (query, ctx) => Promise<MentionItem[] | MentionPage>", description: "Static array or async fetcher", required: true },
	{ name: "markup", type: "string", default: '"{char}[__display__](__id__)"', description: "Markup template (uses trigger char)" },
	{ name: "allowSpaceInQuery", type: "boolean", default: "false", description: "Allow spaces in queries" },
	{ name: "startOfLine", type: "boolean", default: "false", description: "Open only at text start or immediately after a newline (\\n)" },
	{ name: "allowedPrefixes", type: "string[]", default: "undefined", description: "Replace default boundaries with literal allowed preceding Unicode characters" },
	{ name: "minChars", type: "number", default: "0", description: "Min chars before suggestions" },
	{ name: "debounce", type: "number", default: "200", description: "Debounce ms for async fetchers" },
	{ name: "maxSuggestions", type: "number", description: "Cap the entire displayed list across groups and loaded pages" },
	{ name: "color", type: "string", description: "Mention highlight color" },
];

const contextProps = [
	{ name: "cursor", type: "string | number | undefined", description: "Previous page cursor; undefined for a new query" },
	{ name: "signal", type: "AbortSignal | undefined", description: "Cancellation signal for the active request" },
	{ name: "textBefore", type: "string", description: "Plain text before the trigger" },
	{ name: "textAfter", type: "string", description: "Plain text after the query" },
	{ name: "activeMentions", type: "MentionItem[]", description: "All mentions in the editor" },
	{ name: "fullText", type: "string", description: "Complete plain text" },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Trigger Config">
	<p class="lead">Configure each trigger with its own data source, behavior, and appearance.</p>

	<h2>MentionItem and MentionPage</h2><p><code>MentionItem</code> contains string <code>id</code> and <code>label</code>, optional string <code>group</code>, and custom fields. <code>MentionGroup</code> contains string <code>id</code> and <code>label</code>. <code>MentionPage</code> contains <code>items: MentionItem[]</code>, <code>hasMore: boolean</code> and optional <code>cursor: string | number</code>. These types are exported by core and every adapter.</p><h2>TriggerConfig</h2>
	<PropsTable props={triggerProps} />

	<h2>Where Triggers Open</h2>
	<p><code>startOfLine: true</code> requires the trigger to begin the text or immediately follow <code>\n</code>. Leading spaces, tabs, and a lone carriage return do not count as line starts.</p>
	<p>When <code>allowedPrefixes</code> is undefined, triggers retain the default boundaries: whitespace, CJK characters, and punctuation, with word continuations and email, URL, and path joiners excluded.</p>
	<p>Setting <code>allowedPrefixes</code> replaces that boundary rule for this trigger. Each entry matches the single Unicode code point immediately before the complete trigger, including characters represented by surrogate pairs. Entries are literal characters, not regular expressions or multi-character sequences; Unicode normalization is not applied.</p>
	<p>Text start is always allowed, even with an empty array. <code>allowedPrefixes: []</code> therefore permits opening only at text start. When both options are set, both restrictions must pass: opening after a newline requires <code>"\n"</code> in the prefix list as well as <code>startOfLine: true</code>.</p>
	<Code code={`const triggers = [
  { char: "/", data: commands, startOfLine: true },
  { char: "#", data: tags, allowedPrefixes: [" ", "("] },
  { char: "@", data: users },
];`} />
	<p>These options use the same core detection in React, Vue, Svelte, and Angular. They control opening suggestions; mention insertion and stored markup stay the same.</p>

	<h2>MentionContext</h2>
	<p>Second argument to async fetchers — provides editor context.</p>
	<PropsTable props={contextProps} />

	<h2>Async Data</h2>
	<Code code={`const triggers = [{
  char: "@",
  data: async (query, context) => {
    const res = await fetch(\`/api/users?q=\${query}\`);
    return res.json();
  },
  debounce: 300,
  minChars: 2,
}];`} />
	<p>Debouncing, aborting stale requests, and loading states are handled automatically.</p>

	<h2>Custom Markup</h2>
	<Code code={`{ char: "@", data: users, markup: "{{@__display__:__id__}}" }
// Produces: {{@Alice Johnson:1}}`} />
	<p><code>__display__</code> and <code>__id__</code> are replaced with the selected item's label and id. Delimiter characters are escaped automatically.</p>
</DocsLayout>
